<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaMazon U'Mayim Acharonim — Halachah 5<br>Part 1 of 2 (§§ 1–5)<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE FULL TRANSLATION</span></div>
<div class="lm">Based on <span class="lr">LM I:28</span> — <span class="v">"B'ni Lan Baisa"</span><br>Fallen <i>alafin</i>; fallen <i>Toros</i>; <i>hachnasas orchim</i>; the <i>Mishkan</i> traveling through the desert</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Halachic framework</span>: Based on the <span class="h">Torah</span> <span class="v">"Build us a house"</span> (<span class="lr">Siman 28, Likutay I</span>) — see the entire <span class="h">Torah</span> there.</div>

<div class="p">The general principle: the <span class="h">misnagdim</span> [opponents], etc. — this is because they receive Torah from <span class="h">talmidai chachamim</span> who are <span class="mx">"demons in the form of Jews,"</span> etc. — who have fallen Torah from fallen <span class="h">alafin</span> [thousands/letters <span class="h">alef</span>]. Regarding these <span class="h">alafin</span> it is written about Shlomo: <span class="v">"and he spoke three thousand parables, and his songs were a thousand and five"</span> — for Shlomo merited them in holiness. But a <span class="h">talmid chacham</span> who is a "demon in Jewish form," etc. — it emerges that through this, people fall into great <span class="h">kefiros</span> [heresies], etc. The remedy for this is <span class="v">"I am a worm and not a man, the disgrace of mankind"</span> — the aspect of a worm, through which one defeats one's enemies, for the worm is the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span> [faith], etc. This is the aspect of Avraham, etc. For Avraham — who is <span class="h">Chesed</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">emunah</span> — with this right hand he overcomes his enemies, etc. Through this <span class="h">Chesed</span>, the fallen <span class="h">alafin</span> are rectified, in the aspect of <span class="v">"and does kindness to thousands [la'alafim]."</span> To come to <span class="h">Chesed</span>, one can only come through bringing <span class="h">talmidai chachamim</span> who are <span class="h">tzadikim</span> into one's house — which is as though one offered the <span class="h">korban tamid</span>, as our Sages said. And <span class="h">tamid</span> has the <span class="h">gematria</span> of four <span class="h">alafin</span> — which is the <span class="h">tikkun</span> of the <span class="h">alafin</span>, etc. This is what the Elder of the Academy said: <span class="mx">"Build us a house in the air of the world"</span> — for these people want to establish their <span class="h">avodah</span> through the Torah they hear from such <span class="h">talmidai chachamim</span>, but in truth they have nothing to rely on — it is as if they want to build a house in the air, etc. And he said: <span class="mx">"and he stood between heaven and earth"</span> — the true <span class="h">talmid chacham</span> is between heaven and earth, etc. — see all this there well. All of this is the secret of the intent of <span class="h">Parshas HaTamid</span> — see there well and you will understand. You will see the wonders of the One of perfect knowledge — how He concealed within this the secret intent of the <span class="h">Tamid</span> in a new, wondrous, and awesome way, in His exalted manner, about which it is impossible to speak at all, except to one who is wise and understands the truth on his own. We will not elaborate here.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 1 — <i>Birchas HaMazon</i> After Eating: Sorting the Good from the <i>Pesoless</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the <span class="h">mitzvah</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> after eating. For the essence of all <span class="h">birchos hanehenin</span> [blessings over enjoyments] — and especially <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, which is the main one, being <span class="h">d'Oraisa</span>, from which all other <span class="h">berachos</span> were derived, as our Sages said: <span class="mx">"If he blesses afterward, certainly he should bless beforehand"</span> — the essence of all blessings over food is to sort the <span class="h">berurim</span> [clarifications/sortings].</div>

<div class="p">Through the sin of Adam HaRishon — whose sin was in eating — everything became mixed up, and it was decreed: <span class="v">"by the sweat of your brow you shall eat bread... in sorrow you shall eat."</span> Therefore great toil is needed before one merits to eat in holiness — to sort the food from the <span class="h">kelipah</span> and <span class="h">pesoless</span> [waste/chaff] clinging to it through Adam's sin. This is the aspect of all the blessings over food — to sort the good from the food and expel the <span class="h">pesoless</span> outward. This is <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, the foundation of all <span class="h">birchos hanehenin</span> — to sort the food.</div>

<div class="p">The essential sorting is to extract the good in the food — whose connection is from the Torah drawn through true <span class="h">tzadikim</span> — and to expel the <span class="h">pesoless</span> derived from the Torah of the blemished <span class="h">talmidai chachamim</span> mentioned above, who have fallen Torah from the four fallen <span class="h">alafin</span>. For the food gives life to a person — this is palpably evident. The essential vitality certainly does not come from the bread itself, but from the divine vitality, which is the vitality of Torah clothed within the bread, as it is written: <span class="v">"for not by bread alone does man live,"</span> etc. The essential vitality is from Torah: <span class="v">"for it is your life."</span> Therefore the power and vitality in food to sustain a person comes through the holy Torah.</div>

<div class="p">But through Adam's sin, good and evil became mixed in all things. For in the bread and food there is also the grip of <span class="h">pesoless</span> derived from the fallen Toros mentioned above — the aspect of the advice of the Serpent: <span class="v">"the Serpent deceived me."</span> This is blemished and corrupting teaching that is not truthful — that has no power to guide a person on the straight path. All this derives from Adam's sin. For the essence of his sin was also through blemished fallen Toros — the aspect of the Serpent's counsel. For the Serpent came upon him with great cunning and deception — teaching the woman and Adam a very deep and profound teaching, in a way of wondrous wisdom and intellect, until he deceived him so greatly. For Adam was a great sage of a wondrous level, as is known. But the primordial Serpent, who was very cunning, deceived him through the aforementioned teaching derived from fallen Torah from the fallen <span class="h">alafin</span>. He taught them such teachings — added to the command and subtracted, etc. — and engaged them in conversation as though wanting to guide them rightly. He said: <span class="v">"even though G-d said you shall not eat from any tree of the garden,"</span> etc. He added to the command and thereby subtracted afterward, deceiving them with a false teaching of false analogy. He told them: "Just as there is no death in touching, so there is no death in eating." It emerges that the essential sin of Adam was through the blemished teachings mentioned above — the aspect of fallen Toros from the four fallen <span class="h">alafin</span>. From there derives all the mixture in foods that must be sorted through the <span class="h">berachos</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — to sort the food from the grip of the <span class="h">pesoless</span> derived from the fallen Toros. Therefore <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> has four <span class="h">berachos</span> — including <span class="h">HaTov V'HaMaitiv</span> — corresponding to the four <span class="h">alafin</span>. Through the four <span class="h">berachos</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, one sorts the vitality in the food so it is drawn from the four <span class="h">alafin</span> of holiness, and the <span class="h">pesoless</span> from the fallen <span class="h">alafin</span> is expelled.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 2 — Four Who Opened with "<i>Af</i>": the Serpent, Chief Baker, Korach, Haman</div>

<div class="p">This is what our Sages said: <span class="mx">"Four opened with 'af' [even/also]."</span> They are: the Serpent, who said <span class="v">"even though G-d said,"</span> etc.; the Chief Baker, who said <span class="v">"I too, in my dream,"</span> etc.; the congregation of Korach, who said <span class="v">"even not to a land,"</span> etc.; and Haman, who said <span class="v">"even Esther did not bring,"</span> etc.</div>

<div class="p">All four of their evil views derived from the contamination of the Serpent — from the Serpent's counsel that deceived Adam — drawn from the fallen teachings mentioned above. Therefore they are four, corresponding to the four <span class="h">alafin</span>. They blemished the <span class="h">alafin</span>, and <span class="h">alef</span> became <span class="h">af</span> — the aspect of <span class="h">charon af</span> [fierce anger], the severity of judgment. For the four <span class="h">alafin</span> in holiness are the aspect of true Torah — great kindnesses, the aspect of <span class="v">"a Torah of kindness,"</span> as understood from the aforementioned <span class="h">Torah</span>. But when they are blemished, <span class="h">kefiros</span> and <span class="h">avodah zarah</span> result — the aspect of <span class="h">din</span> and <span class="h">charon af</span>, as our Sages said: <span class="mx">"whenever there is avodah zarah in the world, there is charon af in the world."</span> Therefore all four opened with <span class="h">af</span> — <span class="h">alef</span> became <span class="h">af</span> — for all blemished through the fallen Toros above. Through this they learned untrue teachings and false analogies.</div>

<div class="p">The Serpent said <span class="v">"af ki amar Elokim"</span> — through this he wanted to teach them to permit eating from the Tree of Knowledge. The Chief Baker said <span class="v">"af ani bachalomi"</span> — wanting to compare his dream to that of the Chief Butler, when in truth they were two opposites, as brought in our Sages' words. The congregation of Korach said <span class="v">"af lo el eretz"</span> — wanting to mislead Israel as though Moshe Rabbainu <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span> had deceived them, and they reasoned with a foolish <span class="h">kal vachomer</span>: "If one thread of <span class="h">techailas</span> exempts the <span class="h">tallis</span>," etc. — their essential blemish was through corrupted and fallen teachings. And Haman said <span class="v">"af lo haivi'ah Esther"</span> — reasoning in his mind that it was to his benefit, becoming very arrogant until he wanted to hang Mordechai. In truth, everything was to his detriment — she was heaping coals upon his head by bringing him to the feast, as our Sages said. It emerges that all four blemished by receiving evil teachings from the fallen Toros of the four fallen <span class="h">alafin</span>. Therefore all opened with <span class="h">af</span> — the aspect of false analogy derived from the severity of <span class="h">din</span> and <span class="h">charon af</span>, the source of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra's</span> grip. Therefore they compared things falsely.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 3 — The Four <i>Berachos</i> of <i>Birchas HaMazon</i> in Detail</div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the four <span class="h">berachos</span> of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> in detail. The first <span class="h">berachah</span>, <span class="h">HaZan</span> [Who sustains], corresponds to the aspect of <span class="h">Chesed</span> that must be drawn — through which the four <span class="h">alafin</span> are rectified, as explained in the <span class="h">Torah</span>. This is <span class="h">Birchas HaZan</span> — the drawing of <span class="h">Chesed</span>, as it says there: <span class="v">"Who sustains the entire world with His goodness, with grace, with kindness, and with mercy... for His kindness is forever."</span></div>

<div class="p">The second <span class="h">berachah</span>, <span class="h">Birchas HaAretz</span> [for the Land], is the essential one, as brought in the Midrash — the essential <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>, as it is written: <span class="v">"and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless Hashem your G-d for the land."</span> This <span class="h">berachah</span> is the aspect of the essential drawing of the <span class="h">tikkun</span> of the four <span class="h">alafin</span>, drawn through <span class="h">hachnasas orchim</span> — hosting righteous guests — as explained there. This is the essential aspect of <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — the aspect of <span class="mx">"a guest blesses."</span> This is <span class="h">Birchas HaAretz</span>: through blessing over <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, one draws the holiness of the righteous guests whose entire holiness is the aspect of the holiness of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — <span class="v">"the tzadikim shall inherit the land."</span></div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">berachah</span> of <span class="h">Boneh Yerushalayim</span> [Who builds Yerushalayim], where the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> stood — as mentioned in this <span class="h">berachah</span>: <span class="v">"and for the great and holy House,"</span> etc. — this is the aspect of <span class="h">baisa bain shamaya l'ar'a</span> [a house between heaven and earth] — the drawing of the holy Torah that has permanence, as explained there. For the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> in Yerushalayim is the essential House of permanence, the aspect of <span class="h">baisa bain shamaya l'ar'a</span>. For there is the gate of heaven and there is the foundation of the earth — the <span class="h">Even HaSh'siyah</span> from which the world was founded. It emerges that the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> is the essential house between heaven and earth. Therefore the essential Torah is there — there the <span class="h">Aron</span> stood with the <span class="h">Luchos</span>, and <span class="v">"from Tziyon shall come forth Torah."</span> There the <span class="h">Sanhedrin</span> sat in the <span class="h">Lishkas HaGazis</span>, from where the truth of Torah had to be received: <span class="v">"if a matter is too wondrous for you in judgment... you shall arise and go up to the place."</span> Therefore through <span class="h">Boneh Yerushalayim</span> one draws the holiness of Torah, the aspect of <span class="h">baisa bain shamaya l'ar'a</span>, the holiness of the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The fourth <span class="h">berachah</span>, <span class="h">HaTov V'HaMaitiv</span> [Who is good and does good], is to sort and elevate the good hidden within the Torah of the blemished <span class="h">talmidai chachamim</span> mentioned above. For <span class="mx">"good is hidden among the nations"</span> — one must sort and elevate the good from within it, in the aspect of <span class="mx">"eating the inside and discarding the shell."</span> This is <span class="h">HaTov V'HaMaitiv</span> — to sort and elevate this hidden good.</div>

<div class="p">The opponents and <span class="h">misnagdim</span> — for <span class="h">HaTov V'HaMaitiv</span> was established at Yavneh regarding the slain of Baitar who were given burial. The slain of Baitar had lit candles to celebrate the destruction of the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>, as stated in Midrash Eichah (<span class="h">Parshah</span> <span class="v">"Bila Hashem"</span>). They were <span class="h">misnagdim</span> against Yerushalayim and the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>, where the essential true Torah was. But certainly they too need <span class="h">tikkun</span>, for certainly they had much good — they only erred through evil teachings of the opponents of truth, until they rejoiced and lit candles over the destruction. Their error was because there were wicked people in Yerushalayim. But in truth they certainly sinned greatly — despite everything, they should not have rejoiced over the destruction of the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> where the essential Torah was. They only erred through the evil teachings mentioned above.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore when the dead were given burial — the <span class="h">tikkun</span> of the dead: the evil decomposes in the earth and the good is sorted and ascends to its root and resting place — then they established <span class="h">HaTov V'HaMaitiv</span>. And they established this <span class="h">berachah</span> specifically within <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — which at first glance seems puzzling: what connection has the burial of Baitar's slain to <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span>? But according to the above, it is well understood. The essential sorting of good from <span class="h">kelipah</span> is through eating — through <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> after eating. The essential sorting is to extract the good hidden within the blemished teachings mentioned above — the aspect of the slain of Baitar given burial. Therefore the <span class="h">berachah</span> was established specifically within <span class="h">Birchas HaMazon</span> — <span class="h">HaTov V'HaMaitiv</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 4 — A Practical Exhortation: Pray to Be Saved from False Teachings</div>

<div class="p">The general principle for practical application: one must pray greatly to Hashem to be saved from evil teachings derived from the fallen Toros mentioned above. For very, very many have become sunk in this. For all desire to fear Hashem — especially the young, who have not yet been led astray so much and are not so far from their root, and therefore generally yearn and pine greatly to draw close to the service of Hashem. But many become distant through the evil views and false reasoning of the opponents of truth, who receive the fallen Toros. They turn the words of the living G-d upside down and say it is forbidden to pray with intensity and toil and self-sacrifice. They attribute their views to a great <span class="h">tzadik</span> and hang upon him empty fabrications — for <span class="h">chas v'chalilah</span> to think such a thing about a true <span class="h">tzadik</span>. They fabricate such false reasoning from their hearts, derived from blemished teachings from the fallen <span class="h">alafin</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore: <span class="v">"regarding this, let every devout one pray to You at a time of finding"</span> — that he should merit to find a true person, from whom to receive true teaching drawn from true Torah without any <span class="h">pesoless</span> or falsehood and without any mistaken reasoning at all. For even among simple people, mistaken reasonings that turn truth upside down are found. Especially all the falls that people experience in their minds due to their bad deeds, through which they become more distant from Hashem <span class="h">chas v'shalom</span> — all this is from the blemished teachings mentioned above. The <span class="h">ba'al davar</span> [Adversary] puts into one's heart as though one can no longer draw close to Hashem — such false reasonings enter people's hearts, all derived from the fallen Toros. Therefore one must pray greatly to Hashem to be saved from this.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 5 — Israel's Journey Through the <i>Midbar</i> and the <i>Mishkan</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of Israel's journeying in the <span class="h">midbar</span>. This is the aspect of the <span class="h">Mishkan</span> that traveled before them — disassembled and reassembled each time. For the <span class="h">Mishkan</span> was to rectify the sin of the Golden Calf, as our Sages said. The essential sin of the Calf — <span class="h">avodah zarah</span> — derived from the evil teachings mentioned above, from the fallen <span class="h">alafin</span>. For the <span class="h">airev rav</span> [mixed multitude] deceived them with evil reasoning and evil teachings derived from the contamination of the Serpent's counsel, until they instilled great opposition to Moshe Rabbainu, until they came to complete <span class="h">kefiros</span> and made the Calf. All came through the <span class="h">misnagdim</span> — the <span class="h">airev rav</span> — who deceived them through evil teachings.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore Hashem commanded afterward to make the <span class="h">Mishkan</span>, where the <span class="h">Aron</span> with the <span class="h">Luchos</span> stood — the totality of Torah. The <span class="h">Mishkan</span> went with them in all their journeys. For the essential completeness of Torah is in the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>, where the <span class="h">Aron</span> stood in its designated place from the day of creation — the <span class="h">Even HaSh'siyah</span>. Therefore <span class="v">"from Tziyon Torah goes forth."</span> For there is <span class="h">baisa bain shamaya l'ar'a</span>. But because of Adam's sin, and especially the Calf, it was impossible to come immediately to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> and the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>. Therefore they had to circle through the <span class="h">midbar</span>.</div>

<div class="p">All their wandering in the <span class="h">midbar</span> was to sort and elevate the fallen Toros, which are the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'alma</span> [air of the world] — from which all the wanderings of all people are derived. Everyone is compelled to travel, to be unsettled and wandering outside the home. All is to sort and elevate the fallen Toros, which are the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'alma</span>. For when a person is unsettled on the road, he is as though in <span class="h">avira d'alma</span> — outside his fixed home. When he merits, he sorts through this the good hidden in the fallen Toros that are <span class="h">avira d'alma</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is Israel's journeying in the <span class="h">midbar</span> — in the place of <span class="h">kelipos</span>, <span class="v">"the place of serpent and fiery snake and scorpion and thirst"</span> — to sort the <span class="h">nitzotzos</span> [sparks] from there, i.e. to sort the good of the fallen Toros. Therefore they made the <span class="h">Mishkan</span> there — the aspect of the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span> — but it was not yet fixed in its place. They had to disassemble and reassemble it each time to sort and elevate the fallen Toros. For the principle is: <span class="mx">"judgment is sweetened only at its root."</span> Therefore specifically through the <span class="h">Mishkan</span> with the <span class="h">Aron</span> and <span class="h">Luchos</span> themselves being unsettled with all Israel in the <span class="h">midbar</span>, the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'alma</span> — specifically through this they sorted and elevated the fallen Toros to their root each time, until they were rectified and became true Torah. This is the aspect of all the <span class="h">mitzvos</span> of the holy Torah commanded each time in the <span class="h">midbar</span> at the <span class="h">Ohel Mo'ed</span> — they merited this each time by sorting the fallen Toros to their root.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore all their journeys were recorded in the Torah: <span class="v">"these are the journeys of the children of Israel"</span> — for from all their journeys, Torah was made. In all their journeys they subdued the enemies and foes — the <span class="h">misnagdim</span> of truth — for through traveling in the <span class="h">midbar</span> in such holiness with the <span class="h">Mishkan</span> and <span class="h">Aron</span> going before them, they subdued all <span class="h">kelipos</span> nourished by the fallen Toros. They sorted and elevated the good hidden there. As brought in the holy Zohar: through their walking in the <span class="h">midbar</span>, they trod upon the <span class="h">kelipos</span> — when one sorts the good from within them, the <span class="h">kelipos</span> fall and are nullified.</div>

<div class="p">Afterward, when they encamped and assembled the <span class="h">Mishkan</span> and placed it on its base and brought the <span class="h">Aron</span> with the Torah into its place — then they established and built the Torah that they had gathered and sorted during their travels, elevating the Torah from <span class="h">avira d'alma</span> to <span class="h">baisa</span> between heaven and earth — the <span class="h">Bais HaMikdash</span>, which is the <span class="h">Mishkan</span> at the time of its assembly. For <span class="mx">"the Mishkan is called Mikdash,"</span> as our Sages said. They only needed to disassemble it each time and carry and travel with it to subdue the enemies that are the aspect of <span class="h">avira d'alma</span>, by sorting and elevating the fallen Toros from the fallen <span class="h">alafin</span>. But afterward they assembled it in its place, and there the <span class="h">alafin</span> — the aforementioned Toros — returned to their place, sorted and elevated to their root, and were included in the holy Torah commanded each time in the <span class="h">midbar</span> at the <span class="h">Ohel Mo'ed</span>.</div>

